# Commands run by the launchd job com.hakios.demo (RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.metalsoftpipe).
#
# The same draw as rc.jobs.metaldraw, with the compiler library's rasterizer in plain C
# (RWA_SOFTWARE=1) instead of panfrost. The reference words this test compares against were
# produced this way, so "THE SAME" here says the whole Metal -> runtime -> library -> UBO
# binding chain is right and the difference is in the GPU driver.
#
# v12's NIR dump found the real shape of the failure: clearFragment20 does not write a constant,
# it stores what it loads from UBO 14 at offset 16. The test fills that buffer with
# (i * 7 + 13) & 0xff, and the pixel came back 0 for all four words, so the UBO reached the
# shader as zeros. On softpipe the UBO is filled from the same buffers by the same bind_stage.
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 40
/redwood/bin/say_run /redwood/bin/metal_props show
/redwood/bin/say_run /redwood/bin/metal_props on
/redwood/bin/say_run /redwood/bin/metal_drv_test --env RWA_SOFTWARE=1 --draw --fragment clearFragment20 /System/Library/Extensions/AppleMetalGLRenderer.bundle/default.metallib
/redwood/bin/say_run /redwood/bin/metal_props off
